WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:02.501
- Thanksgiving is fast
approaching and I wanna know,

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.840
will my waistband influence

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.861
how much food I can shove in my face?

00:00:05.861 --> 00:00:06.980
This is Brendan.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.741
Brendan agreed to eat a Thanksgiving meal,

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:09.741
three days this week.

00:00:09.741 --> 00:00:11.301
- How did you get the
bigger lab coat than me?

00:00:11.301 --> 00:00:12.134
- Shut up.

00:00:12.134 --> 00:00:13.080
Each day he'll be wearing

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.493
a waistband with different tightness.

00:00:15.493 --> 00:00:16.993
Jeans, sweatpants,

00:00:17.872 --> 00:00:19.221
and a dress.

00:00:19.221 --> 00:00:20.731
We'll determine if his waistband effects

00:00:20.731 --> 00:00:22.821
how much food he can push down his throat.

00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:25.181
At each meal, Brendan will
have a cup of stuffing,

00:00:25.181 --> 00:00:28.291
a cup of mashed potatoes,
a can of cranberries,

00:00:28.291 --> 00:00:30.659
four bread rolls, a whole pumpkin pie,

00:00:30.659 --> 00:00:33.152
and a pound of sliced deli turkey meat.

00:00:33.152 --> 00:00:35.741
Because markets didn't
have whole cooked turkeys

00:00:35.741 --> 00:00:36.992
at the time we shot this.

00:00:36.992 --> 00:00:37.825
At the end of the meal,

00:00:37.825 --> 00:00:39.318
we'll determine how much food he ate.

00:00:39.318 --> 00:00:40.790
And at the end of this experiment,

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.280
we'll know with which waistband

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.090
he was able to eat the most food.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.911
Let's eat.
- Gobble, gobble.

00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:49.384
(lighthearted music)

00:00:49.384 --> 00:00:51.967
(sign squeaks)

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.309
Normal on Thanksgiving, I go ham.

00:00:55.309 --> 00:00:56.800
Well, turkey, I guess.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.419
(drum roll banging)

00:00:58.419 --> 00:01:00.257
But I eat as much as I can.

00:01:00.257 --> 00:01:03.248
You guys just gonna hang out
and watch me eat for awhile?

00:01:03.248 --> 00:01:05.309
All right, easily my favorite things,

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:06.699
Thanksgiving food wise,

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.400
of pumpkin pie and the cranberry sauce.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.459
I like the sweet stuff.

00:01:09.459 --> 00:01:13.568
So a lot people are very
divided on the cranberry debate.

00:01:13.568 --> 00:01:16.560
A lot of people are grossed
out by the jellied kind,

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.886
that's just canned shaped.

00:01:17.886 --> 00:01:19.568
There are a few things I love more

00:01:19.568 --> 00:01:22.256
than a good old can shape
of jellied cranberry sauce.

00:01:22.256 --> 00:01:23.716
Barely food, it's delicious.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.585
(upbeat music)

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.126
I'm definitely feeling it.

00:01:27.126 --> 00:01:28.503
I'm feeling the bloat a little bit.

00:01:28.503 --> 00:01:30.297
I still got more room,
I'm not stopping yet.

00:01:30.297 --> 00:01:32.046
I feel like my comfort
level would be higher

00:01:32.046 --> 00:01:33.806
if I were wearing sweatpants right now.

00:01:33.806 --> 00:01:37.035
'Cause I already feel
that unforgiving waistband

00:01:37.035 --> 00:01:41.628
of the jeans just cutting
into my rapidly expanding gut.

00:01:41.628 --> 00:01:44.297
(belches)

00:01:44.297 --> 00:01:47.535
That being said, I'm gonna
eat some of this pie.

00:01:47.535 --> 00:01:49.209
Pumpkin pie is my absolute

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.617
favorite thing about Thanksgiving.

00:01:50.617 --> 00:01:52.388
I also typically just
like to eat the filling

00:01:52.388 --> 00:01:54.055
and leave the crust.

00:01:57.266 --> 00:01:58.401
It's not weird at all.

00:01:58.401 --> 00:02:01.060
Lots of people eat the
filling and not the crust.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.509
This is a documented thing,
there's millions of us.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:05.252
I'm at that point, that
you have in big meal,

00:02:05.252 --> 00:02:07.361
where your brain's like,
"You're done, you're good."

00:02:07.361 --> 00:02:08.550
And you're like, "No, I'm fine."

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:09.412
And you keep eating.

00:02:09.412 --> 00:02:11.252
I, by any reasonable measure,

00:02:11.252 --> 00:02:12.721
should stop eating right now.

00:02:12.721 --> 00:02:15.081
But I have no intention
to 'cause it's delicious.

00:02:15.081 --> 00:02:16.851
I'm barely even enjoying this pie now.

00:02:16.851 --> 00:02:18.190
But I can't stop eating it.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:19.380
I'm high on pie, I don't know.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.310
Yeah, this stuff's gross.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.913
Oh, I'm gonna call it
actually on that one.

00:02:21.913 --> 00:02:24.270
I feel like I did pretty well.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:27.110
I physically could fit a little more food.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.452
But I am woefully uncomfortable already.

00:02:29.452 --> 00:02:31.000
(belches)

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.561
I am getting paid today to come to work

00:02:33.561 --> 00:02:35.870
in sweatpants and eat a
bunch of Thanksgiving food.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.430
I am free from the clutches of denim.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:41.160
Strategy today, I'm gonna try
to mix it up a little bit.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.910
Today, I'm gonna hit the
turkey a little harder.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.669
I might eat a roll, I don't know.

00:02:44.669 --> 00:02:45.820
I don't want to get ahead of myself.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:47.008
I feel like sweatpants are like

00:02:47.008 --> 00:02:49.929
a magical talisman that you put on

00:02:49.929 --> 00:02:51.940
and then you can suddenly
fit more food in your body.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.773
(energetic music)

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.441
A luxury, baby.

00:02:57.441 --> 00:03:00.721
I already, at this point, haven
eaten quite a bit of food,

00:03:00.721 --> 00:03:02.249
feel exponentially more comfortable

00:03:02.249 --> 00:03:03.460
than I did in the jeans.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:06.293
(energetic music)

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:12.549
I think I'm done.

00:03:12.549 --> 00:03:15.041
I ate more food but I feel just more,

00:03:15.041 --> 00:03:18.353
just kind of like ready for a
nap, as opposed to miserable.

00:03:18.353 --> 00:03:21.060
I am super excited to
see how dress day goes

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.418
so I will see you tomorrow.

00:03:22.418 --> 00:03:24.243
I have never worn a dress before.

00:03:24.243 --> 00:03:26.934
Turns out they are
luxuriously comfortable.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.641
I feel like this is
gonna blow the sweatpants

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.622
and definitely the jeans out of the water.

00:03:30.622 --> 00:03:33.752
But America, we gotta adopt
more dresses for dudes.

00:03:33.752 --> 00:03:34.974
This is fantastic.

00:03:34.974 --> 00:03:36.301
Today, no strategy.

00:03:36.301 --> 00:03:38.283
My only strategy is I'm gonna eat

00:03:38.283 --> 00:03:40.782
all of the food I can and see
where this dress takes me.

00:03:40.782 --> 00:03:42.622
♪ Turkey time ♪

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:45.203
Well, it turns out Thanksgiving
food, still delicious.

00:03:45.203 --> 00:03:46.283
I'm very thankful, obviously,

00:03:46.283 --> 00:03:48.101
for friends and family and loved ones

00:03:48.101 --> 00:03:49.214
and all of the important stuff.

00:03:49.214 --> 00:03:52.312
But this year, I'm mostly
thankful for this dress.

00:03:52.312 --> 00:03:53.803
I'm gonna hit the bread, I'm
gonna hit the bread early.

00:03:53.803 --> 00:03:55.301
I haven't hit the bread this early

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.542
in either of the other meals.

00:03:56.542 --> 00:03:58.152
Why am I hitting it so early?

00:03:58.152 --> 00:04:01.574
Dress.
(gentle music)

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.854
Compared to the last two days,

00:04:02.854 --> 00:04:03.951
at this point in the meal,

00:04:03.951 --> 00:04:05.902
I feel way better than
I felt the other two.

00:04:05.902 --> 00:04:06.782
The first two days--

00:04:06.782 --> 00:04:08.174
Yeah, even in the sweatpants,

00:04:08.174 --> 00:04:10.243
I still felt that bloat coming in,

00:04:10.243 --> 00:04:11.582
that tightness around the waist.

00:04:11.582 --> 00:04:12.603
I don't feel that at all right now.

00:04:12.603 --> 00:04:13.734
I feel like I'm eating naked,

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.222
which would be another cool thing to try.

00:04:15.222 --> 00:04:16.534
This is seriously fantastic.

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:19.094
I feel like I could accomplish
anything in this dress.

00:04:19.094 --> 00:04:21.062
Is this what women feel like all the time?

00:04:21.062 --> 00:04:23.323
(upbeat music)

00:04:23.323 --> 00:04:25.352
Pie is good, but again,

00:04:25.352 --> 00:04:27.192
it's not as good as my mom's pumpkin pie.

00:04:27.192 --> 00:04:28.580
Shout out to my mom.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.912
(upbeat music)

00:04:30.912 --> 00:04:32.182
So today in the dress,

00:04:32.182 --> 00:04:34.462
I was able to eat all
of the mashed potatoes,

00:04:34.462 --> 00:04:37.123
all the stuffing, half the turkey,

00:04:37.123 --> 00:04:40.323
about three quarters of
the can of cranberry sauce,

00:04:40.323 --> 00:04:43.222
and probably about a little
over a quarter of the pie.

00:04:43.222 --> 00:04:47.152
I do feel like I ate the most
amount of food in the dress

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:48.694
and was still the most comfortable

00:04:48.694 --> 00:04:49.992
out of the three outfits.

00:04:49.992 --> 00:04:51.272
- After calculating our numbers,

00:04:51.272 --> 00:04:54.422
and taking Brendan's comfort
level into consideration,

00:04:54.422 --> 00:04:57.622
the winner of the waistband
Thanksgiving experiment

00:04:57.622 --> 00:04:59.152
is the dress.

00:04:59.152 --> 00:05:01.006
(audience cheers)

00:05:01.006 --> 00:05:03.604
Brendan, how do these results
compare with your experience?

00:05:03.604 --> 00:05:05.432
- The dress made a huge difference.

00:05:05.432 --> 00:05:07.272
Not just in how much I was able to eat,

00:05:07.272 --> 00:05:09.580
but also how comfortable
I was while eating.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.683
- There you have it, folks.

00:05:10.683 --> 00:05:12.462
Wear whatever the hell
you want to Thanksgiving.

00:05:12.462 --> 00:05:13.331
You're just gonna shove

00:05:13.331 --> 00:05:14.862
your face full of food regardless.

00:05:14.862 --> 00:05:17.291
- But wear a dress,
definitely, wear a dress.

00:05:17.291 --> 00:05:19.874
(upbeat music)

00:05:33.851 --> 00:05:35.065
(sign squeaks)

